<article class="env-definition" id="05H9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05H9">Definition <span data-tag="05H9">38.4.6</span>.</a> Let $S$, $X$, $\mathcal{F}$, $x$, $s$ be as in Definition <a href="/tag/05H5" data-tag="05H5">38.4.2</a>. Let $(Z, Y, i, \pi , \mathcal{G}, z, y)$ be a one step dévissage of $\mathcal{F}/X/S$ at $x$. Let us define a <em>standard shrinking</em> of this situation to be given by standard opens $S' \subset S$, $X' \subset X$, $Z' \subset Z$, and $Y' \subset Y$ such that $s \in S'$, $x \in X'$, $z \in Z'$, and $y \in Y'$ and such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (Z', Y', i|_{Z'}, \pi |_{Z'}, \mathcal{G}|_{Z'}, z, y)  \]
</div>
  <p> is a one step dévissage of $\mathcal{F}|_{X'}/X'/S'$ at $x$. </p>
</article>